Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

&amp;nbsp;






 PRINTERSCLAN





 &amp;nbsp;





 &amp;nbsp;


 &amp;nbsp;



 Dear Suzie We hope this email finds you well.
 We appreciate you reaching out about issues with your
 Epson printer
 HJKAS








 Paper Jam




 1. Turn off and unplug the printer





 First, make sure that your printer is turned off.
 This is
 important as you must not prod and poke the printer
 when
 it is turned on. Ensure that all printing jobs have
 been
 cancelled and the printer is turned off at the plug.









 2. Remove all printer paper from the tray and try
 reloading





 One of the most common causes of paper jams is that
 the
 paper has simply not been loaded correctly into the
 printer paper feed. With this in mind, remove any
 paper
 from the tray in order to check for any jams. If you
 do
 see some paper jammed, pull each sheet out of the
 printer slowly until the printer is clear again








 3. Open the rear access door...





 Open the rear access door to ensure that the rollers are
 clear and that there aren’t any smaller scraps of paper
 left
 behind.







 4. Plug in and restart the printer.










 &amp;nbsp;





 If your issue is still not resolved or you&#039;re unable to follow these
 instructions, contact our troubleshooting experts, who will diagnose the
 specific problem you&#039;re facing. Our certified experts will help you resolve
 the issue over the phone CALL OUR EXPERTS +1-512-885-1530.










 &amp;nbsp;




 &amp;copy; https://printersclan.com



 &amp;nbsp;


--B_ALT_6816688ac97190.45353138
